## Kynetic-Spec Codebase Exploration Report

### Executive Summary

I've conducted a thorough exploration of the kynetic-spec project structure, focusing on ralph command functionality, agent runtime systems, dispatch engine, and related test infrastructure. The codebase is well-organized with clear separation of concerns: CLI commands in `src/cli/commands/`, core agent/dispatch logic in `src/agent-runtime/`, and ralph-specific functionality in `src/ralph/`. Below is a detailed breakdown organized by area.

---

## 1. Ralph Command Structure (`src/cli/commands/ralph.ts`)

**File Size:** ~2,250 lines of code

**Key Exports & Subcommands:**
- `registerRalphCommand(program)` - Main registration function
- Two subcommands:
  1. **`ralph end-loop`** - Signal to gracefully end the loop (lines 1265-1303)
  2. **`ralph run`** (default) - Main execution with extensive options (lines 1306-2257)

**Core Capabilities:**
- Full loop orchestration with configurable iterations, retries, and failure handling
- Per-role adapter support: `--worker-adapter` and `--reviewer-adapter` for task-work vs PR review
- Explicit task scoping: `--tasks @ref1,@ref2` to limit work to specific tasks
- Iteration timeout: `--iteration-timeout <minutes>` for safety
- Session budget integration: `--max-tasks` creates `budget.json` for tracking
- Streaming session updates with event logging
- Terminal command execution with artifact capture
- Subagent spawning for PR review tasks
- Wrap-up agent on loop exit

**Key Functions:**

| Function | Purpose | Lines |
|----------|---------|-------|
| `parseExplicitTasks()` | Parse and validate `--tasks` flag (AC 21) | 110-143 |
| `filterByExplicitTasks()` | Filter session context to explicit scope | 149-165 |
| `buildTaskWorkPrompt()` | Build iteration prompt with focus & scope (AC 1-3) | 416-484 |
| `buildReflectPrompt()` | Build post-task reflection prompt | 490-522 |
| `runTerminalCommandWithArtifacts()` | Execute shell with bounded preview & artifact streaming | 676-779 |
| `handleRequest()` | Tool request handler (file I/O, terminal, permissions) | 787-872 |
| `processPendingReviewTasks()` | Spawn review subagents (AC 6-12) | 1116-1254 |
| `handleIterationFailure()` | Track per-task failures with escalation (AC 1-8) | 1018-1110 |

**Session Management:**
- Creates session with `KSPEC_SESSION_ID` and `KSPEC_RALPH_SESSION` env vars
- Uses `createSessionWithBudget()` when `--max-tasks` specified
- Streams session updates to event log via `appendEvent()`
- Cleans up budget via `removeEnvForAdapter()` on all exit paths
- Signal handlers (SIGINT/SIGTERM) trigger graceful cleanup in finally block

