## 10. Architecture & Key Patterns

### Session Management Flow:

```
kspec ralph run
  ↓
initContext() → loadMetaContext() → load agents & skills
  ↓
createSessionWithBudget() → create session dir + budget.json
  ↓
injectEnvForAdapter() → set KSPEC_SESSION_ID in harness config
  ↓
for each iteration:
  ├─ gatherSessionContext() → ready/active/pending_review tasks
  ├─ processPendingReviewTasks() → spawn review subagent per task
  ├─ spawnAndInitialize(workerAdapter) → create ACP agent
  ├─ agent.client.newSession() → fresh ACP session per iteration
  ├─ agent.client.prompt() → task-work phase
  ├─ agent.client.prompt() → reflect phase
  ├─ check for iteration timeout
  └─ on failure: handleIterationFailure() → track per-task
  ├─ runWrapUpAgent() → exit summary
  └─ closeSession() + removeEnvForAdapter() → cleanup
```

### Dispatch Engine Flow:

```
DispatchEngine.start()
  ↓
_bootstrap() → evaluate all current tasks against rules
  ↓
External event: handleStateChange() | handleFileChange()
  ↓
_matchesFilter() → check automation, tags, priority
  ↓
_enqueue() → per-agent queue
  ↓
_drainQueues() → spawn up to max_concurrent per agent
  ↓
_spawnInvocation() → runInvocation() in shadowMutex
  ↓
retry on error (AC-9, AC-10)
```

### Skill Invocation Resolution:

```
resolveRalphSkillInvocation(invocation, platform, skillOrigins)
  ↓
tokenResolved = resolveSkillReferenceTokensForPlatform()
  └─ {skill:id} → /kspec:id (claude-code) or $kspec-id (codex)
  ↓
normalizeLegacyInvocation() → backward compat
  └─ /kspec:foo ↔ $kspec-foo per platform
```

